    Gio.File or Gio.InputStream, so the buffer is set as “unmodified”, that is,
    Gtk.TextBuffer.set_modified() is called with False. If the contents isn't
    saved somewhere (for example if you load from stdin), then you should
    probably call Gtk.TextBuffer.set_modified() with True after calling
    FileLoader.load_finish().
